{"name":"My Guinea Pig","hex":"#cbb698","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"guinea","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A gold coin originally worth twenty shillings; later (from 1717 until the adoption of decimal currency) standardised at a value of twenty-one shillings.","Synonym of guinea fowl."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/guinea"},{"term":"pig","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["ISO 639-3 language code for Pisabo."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any of several mammalian species of the family Suidae, having cloven hooves, bristles and a snout adapted for digging; especially the domesticated animal Sus domesticus.","A young swine, a piglet ."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pig"}],"entries":[{"title":"Guinea pig","blocks":[{"text":"The guinea pig, also known as the domestic guinea pig, cavy or domestic cavy, is a species of rodent. It belongs to the genus Cavia, family Caviidae, and its closest wild relatives include the montane guinea pig. Domestic guinea pigs typically weigh between 700 and 1,200 g and measure between 20 and 25 cm in length; most breeds have fur, and they have long front teeth that grow continuously, leading the animals to chew regularly to wear them down. They are social animals, and are skittish in response to noise or danger, evincing a freeze or flight strategy."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/30/George_the_amazing_guinea_pig.jpg/330px-George_the_amazing_guinea_pig.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Guinea_pig","wikidata":"Q79803"},{"title":"Guinea","blocks":[{"text":"Guinea, officially the Republic of Guinea, is a coastal country located in West Africa. It borders the Atlantic Ocean to the west, Guinea-Bissau to the northwest, Senegal to the north, Mali to the northeast, Ivory Coast to the southeast, and Sierra Leone and Liberia to the south. It is sometimes referred to as Guinea-Conakry, after its capital Conakry, to distinguish it from other territories in the eponymous region, such as Guinea-Bissau and Equatorial Guinea. At the census held on 1 July 2025, Guinea had a population of over 17.5 million and an area of 245,857 square kilometres (94,926 sq mi)."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ed/Flag_of_Guinea.svg/330px-Flag_of_Guinea.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Guinea","wikidata":"Q1006"},{"title":"Pig","blocks":[{"text":"The pig, also called swine or hog, is an omnivorous, domesticated, even-toed, hoofed mammal. It is named the domestic pig when distinguishing it from other members of the genus Sus. Some authorities consider it a subspecies of Sus scrofa ; other authorities consider it a distinct species. Pigs were domesticated independently twice during the Neolithic, in the Near East around the Tigris Basin, and in China. When domesticated pigs arrived in Europe from the Near East, they extensively interbred with wild boar in Europe but retained their domesticated features."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3e/Pig_farm_Vampula_1.jpg/330px-Pig_farm_Vampula_1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pig","wikidata":"Q787"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b2/Guinea_pig_skull._Cavia_porcellus_02.jpg/500px-Guinea_pig_skull._Cavia_porcellus_02.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b2/Guinea_pig_skull._Cavia_porcellus_02.jpg/1280px-Guinea_pig_skull._Cavia_porcellus_02.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b2/Guinea_pig_skull._Cavia_porcellus_02.jpg/500px-Guinea_pig_skull._Cavia_porcellus_02.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Skull of a guinea pig","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AGuinea_pig_skull._Cavia_porcellus_02.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bf/Three_Unknown_Elizabethan_Children.jpg/500px-Three_Unknown_Elizabethan_Children.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bf/Three_Unknown_Elizabethan_Children.jpg/1280px-Three_Unknown_Elizabethan_Children.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bf/Three_Unknown_Elizabethan_Children.jpg/500px-Three_Unknown_Elizabethan_Children.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"c. 1580 painting of Elizabethan children with a cavy pet","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AThree_Unknown_Elizabethan_Children.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5a/Nibbles_and_strips_2.jpg/500px-Nibbles_and_strips_2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5a/Nibbles_and_strips_2.jpg/500px-Nibbles_and_strips_2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Parti-colored Abyssinian guinea pigs","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ANibbles_and_strips_2.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/17/Three_guinea_pigs_%28Cavia_porcellus%29_at_Keswick_Public_Library.jpg/500px-Three_guinea_pigs_%28Cavia_porcellus%29_at_Keswick_Public_Library.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/17/Three_guinea_pigs_%28Cavia_porcellus%29_at_Keswick_Public_Library.jpg/1280px-Three_guinea_pigs_%28Cavia_porcellus%29_